          "start_line":271
        }
      ],
      "key":"sprint_close_conditions",
      "statement":"Begin by setting the manifest to closing and freeze new iterations. Review every included ticket or iteration entry against the manifest; check evidence durability; walk changed surfaces against cited authority; classify deferred compliance; and open paydown tickets for surviving debt. Every reviewed item takes one of the six classifications under sprint authority, consuming but remaining separate from assessment results and taking exactly one core value for its acceptance predicate. Closed requires an outcome for every item and every debt entry and durable resulting paydown/repricing work; it does not require every outcome to be satisfied. Hidden authority drift cannot be accepted. The mappings add neither a disposition nor a core value, and consumers cannot treat remaining debt, repricing or removal as compliance.",
      "uncertainty":""
    },
