          "end_line":366,
          "quote":"The rule governs backlog and active tickets; it is not\nretroactive for completed tickets unless a completed ticket is reopened or\nexplicitly repriced. It does not make every ticket multi-tenant: tenant\nduplication is used only when the same admitted work item genuinely has\nmore than one tenant execution line (P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/TICKETS.md#TICKETS%2F4.%20Ticket%20rules%2FMulti-build-tenant%20independence",
          "start_line":362
        }
      ],
      "key":"tenant_lifecycle_independence",
      "statement":"Retain the upstream source/product/design ticket as its own authority surface and create one tenant-local ticket per build tenant, appending a tenant mnemonic to base id and filename. Status, proof, closure, repricing and reopening remain independent; one ticket cannot close more than one tenant lifecycle, and another tenant's green status cannot hide a blocker or false closure. Existing tenant duplicates should record source_ticket and build_tenant; build_tenant identifies the product's how.build_tenants entry, not an unbound alias. The unsuffixed base may remain upstream authority. Upstream-only and single-tenant work require no sibling duplication. This clause owns work-item/lifecycle relations in the consumed context, not tenant identity or realisation meaning.",
      "uncertainty":""
    },
    {
